(3065, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: 

You begin <vocabulary>to count</vocabulary> vocabulary words. You''re out of control and you can''t stop. One after another. Scientists have to come in, but they can''t figure out the <reading>cause</reading> (かぞ) of your counting. They drag you away to a padded cell where they keep testing you trying to figure out the cause of your craziness.'),
(3066, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun''yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn''t learn that reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you with this word: 

