(3277, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you:

You need <vocabulary>to release</vocabulary> your pet <reading>花</reading> (はな). It''s a monstrous, carnivorous 花 that you keep in a cage in your backyard. You think it''s super cute, but your neighbors say it scares them, so you need <vocabulary>to set free</vocabulary> your beloved 花. Hopefully it doesn''t eat anyone on its way back to the wild.'),
(3278, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(3279, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji. むかし sounds like a kun''yomi reading, doesn''t it? It''s so long.'),
(3280, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The は from 波 rendakus to ぱ, so be careful. Maybe it''s your <reading>pa</reading> who has bad reception every time you try to call him?'),
(3281, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: 

You are going <vocabulary>to pour</vocabulary> some <reading>sauce</reading> (そそ).'),
(3282, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
