(4082, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: I''d like <vocabulary>to announce</vocabulary>... we''re not having one baby, we''re having <reading>two</reading> (つ) babies!'),
(4083, 'Sorry, you only learned the kun''yomi reading with 広. So, think of it this way when you need to remember this word''s meaning: You''re advertising something. It''s a big <vocabulary>advertisement</vocabulary> to advertise how terrible a person <reading>こう</reading>いち is. Come up with some terrible things he''s done so that you can imagine this crazy Koichi advertisement you made and ran on national TV.'),
(4084, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4085, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4086, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4087, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4088, 'The readings are what you''d expect except for きつ getting shortened to きっ and 茶, which has this strange さ reading. To remember that it''s さ instead of ちゃ, think of this <vocabulary>tea house</vocabulary> you''re going in. You think it''s nice and pleasant, and it is for a while... until someone starts working a <reading>saw</reading> (さ) outside, ruining the atmosphere. BEWWEEEEHHHEEEHHHHHE gatatatatatat BWEEEHEEE.'),
(4089, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4090, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4091, 'The reading doesn''t seem like it''s the kanji''s on''yomi reading, but it is. What an oddity! Do you think it''s worth doing a news report on it? Koichi, reporting in on this strange reading that is readable by you right now. Signing off.'),
(4092, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4093, 'The reading is like that of 守る, so if you know the reading of that word you should be able to read this one as well.'),
(4094, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. Knowing 留守 will be important as well.'),
(4095, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
