(4100, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun''yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn''t learn that reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you with this word: 

All we need to shoot a <vocabulary>bow</vocabulary> is <reading>you ''n'' me</reading> (ゆみ). One person holds the bow, the other fires the arrows. Teamwork makes the dream work. Even for shooting bows. Just you ''n'' me.'),
(4101, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4102, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: 

You don''t want <vocabulary>to forget</vocabulary> anything, because forgetting always makes everything <reading>worse</reading> (わす). Forgot your car keys? Now you can''t drive. Forgot someone''s name? Now you have to ask again and it''ll be awkward. All these situations make your day worse, and probably your life worse too.'),
(4103, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4104, 'The reading is all kun''yomi vocab reading, as you can maybe guess from the hiragana sticking out. If you know the readings of the words 下 and 書く separately, you should be able to combine them into one reading. Just don''t forget the rendaku here!'),
(4105, 'The readings come from 書く and 入れる. Combine those two words to get the reading of this word.'),
(4106, 'This uses the kun''yomi readings from the vocab words 書く and 方. So as long as you''re okay with those, you can apply that knowledge over here.'),
(4107, 'The readings come from 書く and 直す. Know those and you''ll know how to read this word too!'),
(4108, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
