If you want to knock over something, you''ll have to go to <reading>tow</reading>n (たお) on it. You''ll never be able to knock down anything if all your efforts are perfunctory. You really gotta go to town on that thing!'),
(4262, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The とう goes to どう, though. Agh, what a <vocabulary>面倒</vocabulary>.'),
(4263, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4264, 'You''ll want to know the words 借りる and 手 to be able to read this one. Combine them to know the reading.'),
(4265, 'The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji. No <vocabulary>thick</vocabulary> books needed to understand this reading, yeah?'),
