(4344, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4345, 'When you try <vocabulary>to fly</vocabulary>, the main thing holding you back is your <reading>toe</reading> (と). It''s like forty pounds and holds you down.'),
(4346, 'When you don''t <vocabulary>really</vocabulary> believe someone, you say, "<reading>Hah</reading> (は)! Nice try, but you''re not fooling anyone." <vocabulary>As was expected</vocabulary>, you saw right through their lies. Hah!'),
(4347, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4348, 'This word has a different reading from the ones you''ve learned so far, so here''s a mnemonic to help you:

After the coyote wrecks your model railroad, he bites you on the head, sending you into an indefinite <reading>coma</reading> (こま). '),
(4349, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4350, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
