(4352, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4353, 'The readings are the vocab readings 手 and 洗う put together.'),
(4354, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It''ll also help if you know the two separate words that make up this longer word.'),
(4355, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4356, 'The readings are the kun''yomi vocab readings (hint is that there''s hiragana sticking out there). So, just make sure you know the word 胸 and 焼く. If you do, you can combine that knowledge into this word, and hopefully not get any heartburn in the process.'),
(4357, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4358, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun''yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn''t learn that reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you with this word: Pretend you''re trying to <kanji>whistle</kanji>, but you can''t. All that comes out is air. You make a "<reading>Fuuuuuuueh</reading>" sound over and over, because you can''t get the whole whistling thing down. Go ahead and pretend to do that (or do it for real).'),
(4359, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4360, 'The reading is the kun''yomi readings put together. Thank 口 for being a body part, which tends to cause this to happen. So, you have 口 (くち) and 笛 (ふえ) put together, though ふえ changes to ぶえ, maybe because you can''t whistle properly? Buuuweeee. Buwwweee.'),
(4361, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. Just watch out for the ひ becoming a び like it did in the word 曜日.'),
(4362, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. Just watch out for the ひ becoming a び like it did in the word 曜日.'),
(4363, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It will help to be able to read 可能 as well.'),
(4364, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4365, 'The readings are both kun''yomi readings of the kanji. The readings come from the word 人 and the だち of 友達, though now it''s たち because it hasn''t been rendaku''d. You like to <reading>touch</reading> (たち) people, you perv.'),
(4366, 'You know how 静か is しずか? Well, this is the same reading as that. Say it in a whisper with me: "<reading>しずしず</reading>." Shhh!'),
(4367, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: 

You decide <vocabulary>to add</vocabulary> something and then <vocabulary>to add</vocabulary> something else, and you end up with quite a <reading>qua</reading>ntity (くわ) of things. Just keep adding and adding forever. What a huge QUANTITY you now have!'),
(4368, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4369, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4370, 'The reading is the same as 焼く, so just use that knowledge and apply it here to be able to read this too.'),
(4371, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4372, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4373, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4374, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4375, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(4376, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The ひょう changes to ぴょう and the はつ gets shortened, though, so just about everything about this word is weird.'),
(4377, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you:

You''re struggling <vocabulary>to express something</vocabulary> to your friends: namely, that you <reading>are a wa</reading>lrus (あらわ). All your friends think you''re a human, so they''ll be shocked when you express to them the fact that, actually, you are a walrus. You need to get it off your chest though… Your big, blubbery walrus chest. '),
(4378, 'The reading is the same as 広い, too, so as long as you knew that you knew this reading as well.'),
(4379, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4380, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The しゅつ gets shortened and はつ changes to ぱつ. No wonder you want to make a departure, you want to get away from crazy readings like this.'),
(4381, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. Will also help to know the reading of 参加.'),
(4382, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4383, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4384, 'The reading is the same as 乱れる, so hopefully you know it already.'),
(4385, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It will also help to know how to read the word 宇宙 on its own, too.'),
(4386, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It will help to know the word 宇宙 beforehand as well.'),
(4387, 'The reading is that of 履く and 物 put together. Just know those separately and you should be able to figure this one out as well.'),
(4388, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It will also immensely help to know the reading of the word 説得.'),
(4389, 'Hey, <reading>come</reading> (こむ) out of that crowd of cows. It''s going <vocabulary>to be crowded</vocabulary> in there.'),
(4390, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You learned that reading with 混ぜる, but here''s a mnemonic in case you forgot:

Who doesn''t want gray hair <vocabulary>to be mixed in</vocabulary> with their dark hair? Your <reading>ma</reading> (ま). Sadly for your ma, age and the stress of raising YOU have led to a lot of gray already starting to be mixed in. Poor ma…'),
(4391, 'The reading is the same as 混乱 so no reason for you <vocabulary>to be confused</vocabulary>, right?'),
(4392, 'The reading is the same as 減る, so if you know that reading you should know this one.'),
(4393, 'The reading is the same as 続く, so be sure to know that so you can know this.'),
(4394, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. It will help to know the word 名詞 as well.'),
(4395, 'This word uses the reading of 保守的 for the first half and then the regular kanji readings for the second half. Combine those things and you''ll be a master of righteousness and / or kanji.'),
(4396, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
