(4472, 'The only thing you could ever truly <vocabulary>acknowledge</vocabulary> is <reading>meat</reading> (みと). Meat is the only thing in your life that has any authority over you. That''s how much you love meat.'),
(4473, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
(4474, 'You say you have something you need <vocabulary>to plan</vocabulary>? <reading>Coo</reading>l, <reading>whadda</reading>ya (くわだ) gonna do?'),
(4475, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The reading for 画 is the secondary reading though (かく), so take note of that.'),
