(4498, 'The 誕 reading is what you''d expect. But for 生, this uses the slightly less common secondary reading, so here’s a mnemonic to help you:

Just imagine the <vocabulary>birth</vocabulary> of your friend <reading>Joe</reading> (じょう), the local farmhand. He’s such a massive guy, it must have been quite the ordeal...'),
(4499, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: When you go <vocabulary>to undress</vocabulary> your goal is to become <reading>nu</reading>de (ぬ).'),
