(4627, 'The reading for this one is a bit difficult, but there''s a hint in the kanji. See the 道 in there on the top? What''s the reading for the vocab version of that kanji? It''s みち. That''s the first part. Now, who are you leading? Let''s say you''re leading a bee back to its nest, via the road. It''s a <reading>道 Bee</reading> (みちび)!'),
(4628, 'The reading is the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should know them both already!'),
(4629, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you remember: 

