(4858, 'URGH! The reading isn''t even the same as 断る, how frustrating. <vocabulary>to cut off</vocabulary> is read as たつ. Instead of eating too many chocolates and getting cut off, maybe you''re eating too many tater <reading>tots</reading> (たつ). Don''t eat so many of those, it''s unhealthy. You have <vocabulary>to cut off</vocabulary> tater tots from your diet so you don''t get fat.'),
