(4943, 'The reading for 河 makes sense. The reading for 童 however is weird. Since the meaning is "kappa" though you can use that to remember the reading as well. If you don''t know what a kappa is do some research on the internets and figure out about them. It''s interesting, and it will help you to remember this word.'),
(4944, 'The reading for 氷 is the one you didn''t learn. Think of the glacier coming slowly to your door. It rings your doorbell and says <reading>heyo</reading> (ひょう). Note that the か becomes が here.'),
(4945, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The か goes to が, probably while floating down said <vocabulary>canal</vocabulary>.'),
(4946, 'The reading makes no sense, really. Neither kanji readings work. But, if you remember that a river pig is a fugu, you can know the reading is <reading>ふぐ</reading>as well! YOU ARE A BLOWFISH, JESSE!'),
