(5022, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: If you are going <vocabulary>to be at a loss</vocabulary> you''re going to be <reading>mad</reading> (まど) about it, most likely. Nobody likes to feel at a loss, so imagine how mad you feel when you are.'),
