(5152, 'The reading comes from 回復, but you can also figure it out via the readings of the kanji as well.'),
(5153, 'You should speak in a <vocabulary>delicate</vocabulary> and <vocabulary>faint</vocabulary> voice when you <reading>cuss</reading> (かす). So delicate that the cuss words are <vocabulary>indistinct</vocabulary> to other people, even. It''s the only acceptable way to cuss.'),
(5154, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
