(5317, '<vocabulary>To take a picture</vocabulary>, <vocabulary>to take a video</vocabulary>… You "take" all these things. And how do you say "to take" in Japanese? It''s <reading>取る</reading> (とる), which happens to share a reading with this word. Different kanji but related meanings, and exactly the same reading!'),
(5318, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
