(5321, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: 

The one with the <vocabulary>flag</vocabulary> is the Mad <reading>Hatter</reading> (はた). Just imagine looking through a group of people. You have to find the Mad Hatter, and he has to find you. That''s why he offered to wear a flag on his hat.'),
(5322, 'You''ll have to be careful about this one, as it''s actually read with the two kanji''s kun''yomi readings put together, making this しろはた.'),
(5323, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well. The こく gets shortened to こっ, though, so look out for that.'),
