(5343, 'What are you going <vocabulary>to steal</vocabulary>? How about a <reading>noose</reading> (ぬす)? Wait, why are you stealing a noose? That sounds like trouble to me...'),
(5344, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. But 強  has two on''yomi readings, and you haven''t really seen this one yet, so here''s a mnemonic to help you out:

Think about how when you commit a <vocabulary>robbery</vocabulary>, you <reading>go</reading> (ごう) into someone''s house, then you go to jail as well, if you''re caught.'),
