(5360, 'The reading can be the on''yomi for 年 or the kun''yomi. So, you can do either よくねん or よくとし, or preferably both.'),
(5361, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you:

Where you''re from, everyone measures their <vocabulary>height</vocabulary> in <reading>ce</reading>lery (せ). No inches or centimeters for you, it''s celery sticks only. How many celery sticks tall are you?'),
(5362, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
