(5386, 'You''re always going <vocabulary>to make noise</vocabulary> and be boisterous when you eat something <reading>sour</reading> (さわ). Imagine stuffing lemon slices, sour candy, and umeboshi into your mouth. All at once. See how much noise you make? They''re so sour, and they make you so boisterous.'),
(5387, 'This is a jukugo word, which usually means on''yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you''ll know how to read this as well.'),
