(5665, 'Please keep heaping up the food. I want <reading>more</reading> (もる), more, more.'),
(5666, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you to remember: If you walk around on the beach, you''ll get <vocabulary>sand</vocabulary> in your shoes <reading>sooner</reading> (すな) or later.'),
(5667, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.

Note when you stick this onto another word to specify a type of sugar, like きび砂糖 (cane sugar), this gets rendaku''d to ざとう.'),
(5668, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
