(5769, 'The readings are the reading you learned with the kanji 縦 and かき (changes to がき), though the き gets smushed inside the kanji, because it wants to be confusing like that.'),
(5770, 'This is a jukugo word that usually uses the kun''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.

Note however, that there is a less-common on''yomi reading,  じゅうおう, which is used in some idioms. It''s good to know this reading exists, but you probably won''t come across it very often. '),
