(5801, 'Imagine yourself on a path designed <vocabulary>to run alongside</vocabulary> an endless array of <reading>so</reading>ap (そ) bars. As you walk alongside the soap bars, you enjoy their delightful scents. It''s a "scent-sational" promenade with soap bars that leaves you feeling squeaky clean!'),
(5802, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here''s a mnemonic to help you to remember: Think of how this <vocabulary>ground spring</vocabulary> is everyone''s (皆) origin (元). Everyone can use it, it''s the 皆元!'),
