(5885, 'The reading is the kun''yomi readings of these kanji, put together. I suppose it''s because it''s like two separate words put together into one. That makes this word read as <reading>うみがめ</reading>, where the かめ gets rendaku''d.'),
(5886, 'Let''s help <vocabulary>each other</vocabulary>. Maybe if we work <vocabulary>together</vocabulary> we can get rid of this <reading>tagger</reading> (たが) tagging graffiti all over our neighborhood.'),
