(5917, 'I''m not drunk, <reading>yo</reading> (よ). YO. I''m not drunk, yo. YO. Yo, I''m not drunk. Yo.'),
(5918, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You haven''t seen the on''yomi reading for 泥 yet (でい), so here''s a mnemonic to help you out: 

You''ll probably get <vocabulary>dead drunk</vocabulary> if you start drinking in the middle of the <reading>day</reading> (でい). Just try to wait until the day is over, like maybe after work, you know?'),
(5919, 'The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji!'),
(5920, 'The readings are the readings for 酢 and the kun''yomi reading for 物 which you''ve seen quite a bit by now.'),
(5921, 'The reading is the same as you learned with the kanji.'),
(5922, 'The reading is crazy long, but also crazy easy! You know みず means "water," and うみ means "sea." So, you have a "water sea" which is a lake, which is a <reading>みずうみ</reading>.'),
(5923, 'The reading is the kun''yomi readings of 山 and 中, then the on''yomi reading of 湖.'),
