This word can also be read as ままちち, because 継 can take the special reading まま when it''s used as the prefix "step," as in "stepfather."'),
(6001, 'You not only inherit one fortune, but <reading>two</reading>! You''re lucky both sides of your family "accidentally" died at the same time. <reading>TWO</reading> (つ) fortunes! TWO! HAHAHAHA. Also, you can think of it like the つ of 次, because you are the "next" successor when you inherit something.'),
