(6009, 'You want <vocabulary>to step on</vocabulary> that bug? You <reading>foo</reading>l (ふ)! That''s a killer shoe stabbing bug, it will cut right through your sole and poison you via your foot! <reading>Foo</reading>l!'),
(6010, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own. Just remember that the はん changes to ぱん for 般.'),
