(6114, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: The <vocabulary>fragrance</vocabulary> you smell is somebody''s <reading>顔</reading> (かお). Just imagine smelling the fragrance of a bunch of people''s faces. Yum!'),
(6115, 'The reading doesn''t follow any of the rules you might expect. Try to use the meaning mnemonic to get the meaning, then know that it sounds something similar to the reading. "Hon(g) Kon(g)" goes to <reading>ほんこん</reading>. Almost the same, right?'),
