(6431, 'Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun''yomi reading. You didn''t learn that reading with this kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help you: Something that happens <vocabulary>frequently</vocabulary> is something that has really caught on. People want to do this thing frequently, because it is so <reading>chic</reading> (しき).'),
(6432, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6433, 'What is multiplying? Your use of the word "<reading>fu</reading>" (ふ) for when you laugh. You used to say just "ha ha ha" like everyone else. Now the occurrences of you saying <reading>fufufu</reading> is really multiplying. You might also notice that this is similar to the word 増える, which means "to increase." This has a similar meaning and the same reading, use that to your advantage!'),
(6434, 'This drink is way too <vocabulary>dilute</vocabulary>d. <reading>You sue</reading> (うす) the makers for their thin drink.'),
