(6540, 'What’s the key <vocabulary>to arrive at</vocabulary> enlightenment? Being an avid <reading>eater</reading> (いた)! Being an eater of all things delicious will truly let your body and mind arrive at new levels. Give it a shot. Become an eater.'),
(6541, 'You didn''t learn this reading of 夏 with the kanji, so here''s a mnemonic to help:

Just think about how cute little <reading>ge</reading>ckos (げ) start to come out into the open during the summer solstice. It''s too cold for them to be out in the open before that, so if you look outside at the right time, you''ll see geckos popping out of the ground all over the place!'),
(6542, 'The reading for 冬 is the on''yomi reading, and one you haven''t learned before. You''re going to want to think about how you are celebrating the <vocabulary>winter solstice</vocabulary> in one particular place, that place being <reading>とう</reading>きょう. See the Tokyo landmarks around you, think that you are there on the winter solstice, and also think about the things you are doing to celebrate, here in Tokyo. Also, watch out for the rendaku.'),
(6543, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
