(6545, '<vocabulary>Sincerity</vocabulary> and <vocabulary>truth</vocabulary> are so important to me that I always keep them inside <reading>my coat</reading> (まこと). That''s where I keep everything that''s dearest to me, and what could be more important that sincerity and truth? Where do you keep sincerity and truth? I bet your answer is "my coat" too.'),
(6546, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6547, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6548, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6549, 'The reading for 郷 is the one you learned, but the reading for 里 isn''t the one you learned. To remember this reading, just think about how your <vocabulary>birthplace</vocabulary> is the place you were <reading>rea</reading>red (り), and you <reading>rea</reading>lly (り) miss the place.'),
(6550, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.

While こきょう is the more common reading for this word, it can also be read as ふるさと, which is a native Japanese word that originally didn''t have kanji. ふるさと is also common in hiragana. '),
(6551, 'The reading for 帰 is the on''yomi reading, which you haven''t learned. Just think about how when you return to your hometown, you''re going to need a <reading>key</reading> (き) to get into your old home, which you haven''t been to in a long time.'),
(6552, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
