(6721, 'You really don’t want your knee <vocabulary>to be grazed</vocabulary>. If it happens, you are gonna <reading>sue</reading> (す). But the <reading>cos</reading>t (こす) of suing is pretty high, so be careful not to get grazed in the first place!

Depending on which reading you use, the nuance changes slightly. For example, すれる is the usual choice when you’re talking about your grazed knees or worn out jeans. For other uses, they are often interchangeable.'),
(6722, 'The reading is pretty weird, and not one you''ve learned. But, you know what sumo is, right? It''s just the same as that. It''s <reading>すもう</reading>.'),
