(6728, 'You find something that is so <vocabulary>soft</vocabulary> to the touch. You touch it. You can''t stop. The monkey you''re touching tells you to stop. It doesn''t like to be touched. But, you won''t stop. "<reading>Yah wha</reading>t (やわ) you gonna do about it, monkey?" "<reading>Yah, wha</reading>t can I do, I guess," replies the monkey.'),
(6729, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6730, 'You didn''t learn this reading of 柔 with the kanji, so let''s remember it a different way. You have to be <vocabulary>gentle</vocabulary> and <vocabulary>tender</vocabulary> if you want to touch something that''s <reading>new</reading> (にゅう) to this world... a puppy, a kitty, a baby, etc. Anything new needs that <vocabulary>gentleness</vocabulary>.'),
(6731, 'When you sink something, like a battleship, you go on and say: "<reading>she''s</reading> (しず) sunk, I sunk her." That''s like your tagline, or something. You say it for some reason because you think it''s cool.'),
(6732, 'Your boat is about <vocabulary>to sink</vocabulary>, so you run around yelling, "<reading>She''s</reading> (しず) sinking! She''s… she''s sinking! Abandon ship!" Boats are always female, so be careful not to say "it." If you don''t say "she''s" sinking, your crew might not get the message.'),
(6733, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6734, 'The reading is the one you learned with the kanji, ぬま.'),
(6735, 'The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji.'),
(6736, 'The readings are the ones you learned with the respective kanji.'),
(6737, 'The readings are the vocab readings of the two words, 泥 and 沼.'),
(6738, 'Oddly, this is the one word that uses the on''yomi reading, which you didn''t learn with the kanji. To remember this particular <vocabulary>swamp</vocabulary>, note how there are two kanji in here that make this area particularly swampy. Because it''s the swampiest, boggiest place in all of Japan, of course the <reading>Sho</reading>gun (しょう) wants it for himself. Even though it''s useless land, he wants the best of everything, being the Shogun and all.'),
(6739, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6740, 'You are going <vocabulary>to destroy</vocabulary> the <reading>hoe roe</reading>. This is the roe that comes from the hoe tools. If they create too much roe, they will create too many hoes. And if there are too many hoes, bad things will happen.'),
(6741, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
