(6810, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the kun''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6811, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own. Be careful of the shortening and the rendaku.'),
(6812, 'To remember the reading of this, just think about how you start <vocabulary>to shout</vocabulary> and <vocabulary>to scream</vocabulary> when you drink way too much <reading>sake</reading> (さけ).'),
(6813, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own. Careful of the shortening.'),
(6814, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji!'),
