(6817, 'The reading for 髪 isn''t the one you learned. It''s actually はつ, but it''s getting rendaku''d here. So, to remember the reading of it for this word, just think about how if you were <vocabulary>blonde</vocabulary>, you''d wear many <reading>hats</reading> (はつ) to hide it. I have no idea why you''d hide it, but you can come up with a compelling reason that makes sense to you.'),
(6818, 'The readings are the vocab kun''yomi readings, 髪 and 毛, put together.'),
(6819, 'The readings are the vocab readings of the individual kanji. For 髪 that''s no problem. For 型 just remember that it''s the individual vocab reading. Watch out for the rendaku.'),
(6820, 'The reading is the reading you learned with the kanji.'),
(6821, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji.'),
(6822, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6823, 'Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun''yomi reading. You learned this reading with the kanji, but here''s a mnemonic in case you need a refresher:

Your <kanji>teardrop</kanji>s are like little waves. What are they? They''re <reading>波だ</reading> (なみだ).'),
(6824, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You haven''t learned this reading for 涙 yet, so here''s a mnemonic to help you:

Your excessive <vocabulary>tears of emotion</vocabulary> have <reading>rui</reading>ned (るい) your life. Your friends didn''t like being cried at for the smallest compliment or favor, so now they don''t even return your calls. No one else you know is <vocabulary>being moved to tears</vocabulary> on a daily basis like this. It''s ruining your life!'),
(6825, 'The reading is the one you learned with the kanji.'),
(6826, 'The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji. It also just sounds like <reading>can</reading>.'),
(6827, 'This word is a combination of 空く and 缶, so if you know the readings for those, you should be fine here.'),
(6828, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6829, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji.'),
(6830, 'The reading is the reading of 姫 and 様 combined together.'),
(6831, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji.'),
(6832, 'The readings are the ones you learned with the individual kanji. Be careful of the rendaku.'),
(6833, 'These readings are the ones you learned with the kanji. Just keep in mind that 棚 gets rendaku''d to だな.'),
(6834, 'You take all the <vocabulary>grain</vocabulary> and put it in a <reading>tube</reading> (つぶ). Just imagine doing this, grain by grain.'),
(6835, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6836, 'The reading is the on''yomi readings. For 雨, you learned it with 雨天. So you should be able to put them together!'),
(6837, 'To remember the reading think about <vocabulary>thunder</vocabulary>. Back in the day, it was probably terrifyingly loud. Like the cry of the gods! Wait a sec, the "cry of the gods" would be <reading>神鳴り</reading> (かみなり).'),
(6838, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6839, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji.'),
(6840, 'The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
(6841, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.'),
