(7074, 'This is a jukugo word that uses the on''yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own. Just watch out, because this uses the せ, not the せい you''re used to seeing.'),
(7075, 'The readings for both kanji are ones you haven''t seen before. So here''s a mnemonic to help you remember:

So how does Italy attain its <vocabulary>flamboyance</vocabulary>? Because it embodies <reading>Da</reading>n<reading>te</reading>’s (だて) bold essence—vibrant, captivating, and <vocabulary>chic</vocabulary> in every way. In Italy, Dante''s influence is a living testament to flamboyant elegance.'),
