(7102, 'This word uses the on''yomi reading for 紙 even though you went through all that trouble to learn the kun''yomi reading. Did you know <vocabulary>paper money</vocabulary> is made of <reading>shee</reading>p (し)? Well, part sheep, but there''s sheep in there for sure. That''s why you can wash your paper money with your t-shirts in the washing machine.'),
(7103, 'Who do you hold a grudge against the most? That would be <reading>you, Ra</reading> (うら). You and your dumb sun.'),
