(7428, 'The reading of 洞 is one you''ve learned. The reading of 穴 isn''t one you''ve learned, though. So, think about how you go inside this <vocabulary>cave</vocabulary>, only to find yourself covered by some red goopy liquid. You think it''s blood, but luckily it just turns out to be <reading>ketsu</reading>p (けつ). If you want to be less formal, you can also use the kun''yomi and say ほらあな, but then you''d never learn that reading for 穴, and where''s the fun in that?'),
