(7602, 'The reading for this is an exception. The reading for 何 is just the first な from なに. You can remember the second part this way:

No one knows quite <vocabulary>how</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>why</vocabulary> that big <reading>ze</reading>ppelin (ぜ) crashed in the 1930s. People are still asking today and no one has any answers. We have to keep asking until we get some.'),
(7603, 'The readings for this word are both kun''yomi readings. You''ve learned both of these readings by now so you should be able to read this on your own.'),
